{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>And I will cast your carcasses upon the carcasses of your idols.</b> This occurs while the city is under siege, as the Sages recounted (Sanhedrin 63b) regarding Elijah the righteous, who found an infant lying in starvation. When he said to him, 'Say שְׁמַע יִשְׂרָאֵל and you will live,' he replied, 'Silence — not to mention the Name of HaShem.' He drew his fear from his bosom, kissed it, and died upon it."], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:38:15.080814295Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}